WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:12.848
Welcome. This is the voicebot architecture, combining Amazon Connect Customer with a traditional speech-to-text and text-to-speech stack. Let's walk through an example request as it moves through the system.

00:00:13.448 --> 00:00:16.272
First, the caller dials the Amazon Connect number.

00:00:16.872 --> 00:00:22.710
Amazon Connect invokes ElevenLabs to provide text-to-speech using a custom voice model, which greets the caller.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.147
The caller then speaks their request.

00:00:25.748 --> 00:00:30.372
Amazon Connect uses its agentic voice capability to convert the caller's speech into text.

00:00:30.972 --> 00:00:34.460
The resulting text is passed to Amazon Lex for intent recognition.

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:46.185
If the detected intent is a DemoBank question-answering request, Amazon Lex invokes an AWS Lambda function, which in turn calls Amazon Bedrock to generate an answer using retrieval-augmented generation.

00:00:46.785 --> 00:00:54.010
The response is then returned to Amazon Connect, which invokes ElevenLabs to convert the answer back into natural speech and deliver it to the caller.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:59.665
And that completes the example flow through the voicebot architecture. Thanks for watching.
